  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything, because removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` would break ARCH-4.\n\n`OrderPlaced` is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repos. Nothing in this repo reads `channel`, but I can't see whether those services do. Under ARCH-4, removing a field from the event needs a deprecation period, not a straight deletion.\n\nThe order model is tied to the event. `src/core/events.ts:50` fills the event's `channel` from `order.channel`. If I remove it from the model, the event loses the field too.\n\nHere are the options:\n1. **Deprecate first (my recommendation).** Mark `channel` as deprecated on `OrderPlaced` in `src/core/events.ts:16`, and keep populating it. Once billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't use it, remove it in a follow-up change.\n2. **Remove it from the order model and API only.** The event would keep emitting `channel`, so I'd have to give it a fixed placeholder value, which is misleading. I don't recommend this.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now.** Do this only if you can confirm both consumers ignore the field, or if Architecture has approved the break.\n\nThe model change touches `src/core/order.ts`, `src/api/requestParsing.ts` and the tests. `POST /orders` currently requires `channel` and returns 400 when it's missing or invalid. After removal it would accept and ignore the field, so existing clients keep working. `GET /orders/{id}` doesn't return `channel`, so ARCH-8 isn't affected.\n\nWhich option do you want?",
